To decompose the mission description into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we need to identify the main objectives and break them down into sub-goals and tasks. The mission involves collecting resources from storage and delivering them to a specified location, with considerations for battery management and parallel task execution.

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title                  | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|---------|-----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1      | Complete Resource Delivery  | Ensure resources are collected and delivered to the specified location. | -                  | Achieve   | -        | The main mission objective is to achieve successful delivery. |
| G2      | Collect Resources           | Gather required resources from storage locations.                    | #                  | Perform   | G1       | Parallel collection from multiple storages reduces time. |
| G3      | Deliver Resources           | Transport collected resources to the specified location.             | #                  | Perform   | G1       | Parallel delivery can occur if multiple resources are needed. |
| G4      | Manage Battery Levels       | Monitor and manage battery levels during collection and delivery.    | FALLBACK(G4.1, G4.2) | Achieve   | G1       | Fallback ensures mission continuity if battery is low. |
| G5      | Handle Mission Failures     | Trigger alerts and report failures to the sector manager.            | -                  | Perform   | G1       | Ensures accountability and response to failures. |

#### Sub-Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title                  | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|---------|-----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G4.1    | Recharge During Collection  | Return to recharge if battery is below 10% during collection.        | -                  | Perform   | G4       | Ensures robot can continue mission after recharging. |
| G4.2    | Reassign During Delivery    | Return resources to checkpoint and reassign task if battery is below 30% during delivery. | -                  | Perform   | G4       | Prevents resource loss and ensures task completion. |

### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title                  | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location          | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|-----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|-------------------|------------------|---------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage         | Move to the storage location to collect resources.                  | AND      | Storage           | [1, n]           | Multiple robots can be assigned to different storages. |
| AT2     | Request Resources           | Send a message to storage for resource retrieval.                   | AND      | Storage           | 1                | Single robot handles communication with storage. |
| AT3     | Retrieve Resources          | Wait for and collect the specified resources from storage.          | AND      | Storage           | 1                | Single robot retrieves resources. |
| AT4     | Navigate to Delivery Point  | Transport resources to the specified delivery location.             | AND      | Delivery Location | [1, n]           | Multiple robots can deliver different resources. |
| AT5     | Return to Recharge Station  | Move to recharge station if battery is low during collection.       | AND      | Recharge Station  | 1                | Single robot recharges. |
| AT6     | Return Resources to Checkpoint | Return resources to checkpoint if battery is low during delivery. | AND      | Checkpoint        | 1                | Single robot returns resources. |
| AT7     | Trigger Alert               | Send an alert and report to the sector manager in case of failure.  | AND      | Control Center    | 1                | Single robot handles alerting. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3, G4 [AND]**: All sub-goals must be completed for the main goal to be achieved.
  - **Justification**: Collection, delivery, and battery management are all essential for mission success.

- **G2 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [AND]**: All tasks must be completed for resource collection.
  - **Justification**: Navigation, requesting, and retrieval are sequential steps in collection.

- **G3 -> AT4 [AND]**: Delivery task is essential for completing the delivery goal.
  - **Justification**: Transporting resources is the core of the delivery process.

- **G4 -> G4.1, G4.2 [FALLBACK]**: Either recharging or reassigning ensures battery management.
  - **Justification**: Fallback allows for flexibility in handling low battery situations.

- **G4.1 -> AT5 [AND]**: Recharging task is necessary if battery is low during collection.
  - **Justification**: Ensures robot can continue mission after recharging.

- **G4.2 -> AT6 [AND]**: Returning resources to checkpoint is necessary if battery is low during delivery.
  - **Justification**: Prevents resource loss and ensures task completion.

This goal model provides a structured approach to decomposing the mission into manageable objectives and tasks, ensuring efficient execution by multiple robots.
